The `_strip_existing_layers` will strip frontmatter and the title line, keeping everything after (session 1 body + session 2 content). Then it re-wraps with new frontmatter + new title. So the final file will have session 1 + session 2 content under one title. That's the intended "同日多会话追加" behavior.

But wait, there's a subtlety: session 2 content starts with `---` (separator) then `# 会话 2 · ...`. The `_strip_existing_layers` strips the FIRST `---` frontmatter only (via split("---", 2)), then strips the title line. It won't strip my session 2's `---` separator (that's deeper in the body). So my separator stays. Good.

Actually, wait — there's a concern. `_strip_existing_layers` loops: it strips frontmatter (leading ---), then strips title line, repeatedly. After stripping the original frontmatter and title, the remaining body starts with session 1's "## 差异栏..." content. Then my appended content starts with "\n\n---\n\n# 会话 2 · ...". The loop checks `if text.startswith("---")` — after stripping original frontmatter, text starts with "## 差异栏" (session 1), so the loop stops. Good. My session 2 separator `---` is in the middle, not the start, so it's preserved.

Then the re-wrapped file will be:
```
---new frontmatter---
# ouyangfeng · 2026-09-07

## 差异栏 (session 1)
... session 1 full content ...
--- 
# 会话 2 · ...
... session 2 full content ...
```

